{"id":"aa09abb4-c8ad-4430-8d14-107bfd9f720d","object":"chat.completion","created":1784988985,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        cu = core[u]\\n        cv = core[v]\\n        w = max(cu, cv, d)\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst = []\\n    total = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst.append([u, v, w])\\n            total += w\\n    if len(mst) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected\\\")\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst, \\\"total_weight\\\": total}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce the implementation for solve(case) that computes the MST of the mutual reachability graph. The case payload contains nodes, core_distance dict, distances list (each a [node1, node2, distance] triple). We compute mutual reachability weight = max(core_distance[node1], core_distance[node2], distance). Then build edges with (weight, node1, node2) and sort by weight, then by node1, then node2 (canonicalize undirected endpoints: ensure node1 < node2 lexicographically). Then run Kruskal with union-find to select n-1 edges. Return {\"mst_edges\": list of [node1, node2, weight], \"total_weight\": sum of weights}. Must handle edge cases: ensure graph is connected; if not connected, raise ValueError. Also sort each edge's nodes alphabetically (or lexicographically) to canonicalize. The output schema requires prefixItems: [string, string, number] for each edge. So the edges list should be list of triples with node strings and numeric weight. The total_weight is sum.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) in Python. Use standard library only. The function returns dict. Must not mutate case. Use deterministic sorting.\n\nPotential pitfalls: case may have duplicate edges? Not specified but likely not. We'll process all distances. Build adjacency list? No need, just edges list.\n\nUnionFind class with find and union by rank.\n\nImplementation steps:\n1. Extract nodes list, core_dist dict, distances list.\n2. Build list of edges: for each (u,v,d) in distances, compute core_u = core_dist[u], core_v = core_dist[v], weight = max(core_u, core_v, d). Ensure canonical order: if u > v, swap. Append (weight, u, v).\n3. Sort edges: first by weight, then by u, then by v (since already canonical).\n4. Initialize UnionFind with nodes set.\n5. mst_edges = [] ; total = 0.\n6. Iterate sorted edges: if find(u) != find(v), union them, add [u, v, weight] to mst_edges, total += weight.\n7. After loop, if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes)-1, raise ValueError (disconnected).\n8. Return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total}.\n\nEdge cases: nodes may be not contiguous? But we assume from payload. Use set of nodes to initialize union-find.\n\nWe'll encode the Python source as JSON string.\n\nNote: The output structural schema says \"additionalProperties\": false at top level, so only \"mst_edges\" and \"total_weight\" allowed.\n\nNow produce the final JSON response with key \"implementation\" containing the source code string.\n\nMake sure to escape newlines and quotes properly. Use triple quotes or just standard escaping.\n\nLet's write the code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    core = case['core_distance']\n    distances = case['distances']\n    # Build edges\n    edges = []\n    for u, v, d in distances:\n        cu = core[u]\n        cv = core[v]\n        w = max(cu, cv, d)\n        # canonicalize\n        if u > v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\n    # sort\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\n    # union-find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    mst = []\n    total = 0.0\n    for w, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst.append([u, v, w])\n            total += w\n    if len(mst) != len(nodes) - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected\")\n    return {\"mst_edges\": mst, \"total_weight\": total}\n\nThat should work.\n\nPotential floating point issues? Not likely, just sum. Use float.\n\nNow encode as JSON string. We'll write the source string with proper escaping.\n\nLet's generate the final response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":1418,"total_tokens":3435,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1019},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":97},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}